 "notes": "Code editor: about 130 old names reduced to eight archetypes (VS Code with forks, Visual Studio editions, JetBrains family, Xcode, Vim, Emacs, Sublime Text, Notepad++) plus 16 flat; dropped trade/legacy (Rational, JDeveloper, Solaris Studio, Understand, Borland, Turbo Pascal, Flash Builder, Aptana, Xamarin Studio, JBuilder, SlickEdit, Komodo, labs/embedded: LabVIEW, LabWindows). AI coding assistant: 35 to 5 archetypes plus 18; Cursor listed once. Code editor plug-in: 56 to 2 marketplace archetypes plus 17 well-known add-ons; dropped cloud toolkits and dead add-ons (Bracket Pair Colorizer, Nyan Progress Bar, Randomness). Compiler and runtime: about 230 old names reduced to seven archetypes (GCC, Clang/LLVM, MSVC, .NET, OpenJDK, Python, Node.js) plus 10; dropped internal components (RyuJIT, CoreRT, Roslyn, IL2CPU, Bartok), research and vendor-embedded compilers, and dead Lisp/Scheme implementations. Version control: Git, Mercurial, Subversion plus GUI clients; trade systems dropped (ClearCase, StarTeam, PVCS, AccuRev, Dimensions, PTC Integrity, Vault, Surround, IC Manage). Game engine: about 200 old names reduced to nine archetypes and Adventure Game Studio plus 20; in-house studio engines (4A, Frostbite, Decima, Fox, id Tech, REDengine, Snowdrop and similar) trimmed. Web design: four archetypes plus nine; SharePoint Designer dropped (enterprise). WordPress-style builders are not in old data and no retrieved page covers them, so omitted. Windsurf maker taken from old data (Cognition)."
